maya: Node 18.18.0, yarn.lock. Cleared deps and reinstall confirmed same failure. Here's the SDK package.json excerpt from node_modules/redwood-inference-sdk/package.json: 

```
{
  "name": "redwood-inference-sdk",
  "version": "1.2.0",
  "main": "dist/index.cjs.js",
  "module": "dist/index.mjs",
  "types": "dist/index.d.ts",
  "exports": {
    "./package.json": {"default": "./package.json"},
    \".\": {"import": "./dist/index.mjs"}
  }
}
```

Note there is no `require` conditional under `exports`. I think that's the issue for SSR builds that still require CJS.

messages_5:
sarah: Investigated — we mistakenly shipped exports without the `require` conditional in 1.2.0 when trying to prefer native ESM. That breaks older bundler paths. I pushed a canary: redwood-inference-sdk@1.2.1-canary.20260315 which adds: 

```
"exports": {
  \".\": {"import": "./dist/index.mjs", "require": "./dist/index.cjs.js"},
  "./package.json": {"default": "./package.json"}
}
```

Also added `browser` mappings for bundlers that look for a browser field. Please try the canary and report back.

